<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:27.400
CHAPTER 33

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.340
THE FOX'S WEDDING AND HAKUSANBO

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:38.080
Wow. Talk about a rural location.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.270
Was there really
a request from this place?

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:42.110
Yeah.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:46.280
We always act on
letters from the Yokai Mailbox.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:50.910
I suppose we can overlook the useless
Rat Man tagging along uninvited,

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.800
but why are you here, too?

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.370
It looks like the Ring of Arcana
might appear around here.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:58.870
What?

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:04.380
I heard that Kitaro was
headed this way, so I came along.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.550
So you take up requests in letters
from the Yokai Mailbox.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:12.840
Tell me, Kitaro, why do you
go to all this trouble?

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:17.390
It's something of a promise.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:18.890
A promise?

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:21.230
Oh, something's up ahead.

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:23.320
You think that's it?

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.730
We've been expecting you.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:29.820
I'm the owner, Kuzumi.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:34.320
Kitaro-san, I beg of you, please help us.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.740
Well, this is an impressive home.

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.500
Do you have noble ancestry?

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:47.290
No. It just so happened a linear train was
planned though my ancestors' cheap land.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:53.930
I used the money from selling it to
do business and happened to get lucky.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.390
We can probably
squeeze a lot out of this one.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:59.640
Leave negotiations to me.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.730
Keep out of this.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:07.060
You said that your daughter is being
targeted by a nasty <i>yokai</i>.

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:08.920
Yes.

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:13.030
We're coming in, Yayoi.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.010
Yes, Father.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:28.040
Hello. My name is Yayoi Kuzumi.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:31.430
This is all pretty excessive.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:33.890
What are you so afraid of?

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:40.640
Well, you see Yayoi has been targeted
by a <i>yokai</i> calling himself Hakusanbo.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.520
It was about three months ago.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:46.770
An arrow with a letter
was stuck in the gate.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.270
It said he was coming to
take Yayoi on her 18th birthday.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:53.530
Dad, who's the Hakusanbo?

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:57.620
He's the leader of the Yoko
that live in the nearby mountains.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:01.520
It's said he's a <i>yokai</i> who would
kidnap and eat humans.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.830
My daughter has always been unlucky.

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.960
As a child she almost drowned.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:11.420
When she'd go to town,
she'd almost get run over.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:16.680
That's why I protected her
by raising her at home.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:20.220
But it looks like
an evil <i>yokai</i> has set its eyes on her.

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:24.310
I beg of you, please save my daughter!

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.440
I understand.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:30.940
We should probably call the Sand Witch
and have her help with this.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:35.190
We should set up a barrier
and prepare for Hakusanbo.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:43.120
Victor, can't you make predictions for
where the ring appears more efficiently?

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.750
I would if I could.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.380
You could call it a tendency,

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:53.570
but it seems to tend to appear in places
where space-time or causality are warped.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.740
Oh-ho, speak of the devil,
there's a signal.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:07.890
What a strange barrier.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.770
This is how it's done in Japan.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.900
I suppose it's different from
your Western magic.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:16.450
But it's nothing to scoff at.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:21.300
This barrier neutralizes all
<i>yokai</i> activity and spirit power.

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:24.970
I'm sorry. All this for someone like me.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:29.000
Could you lay off the
"someone like me" stuff?

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.000
It kills my motivation.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.730
Have I offended you somehow?

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:38.890
It's just that I've never had
any friends before.

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.970
I don't really understand.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:44.890
Never had any friends?
What about at school?

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:47.470
We hired a tutor to come to our house.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:51.980
Wait, are you saying you really
never leave your house?

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:54.610
Talk about sheltered.

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:59.610
It may not seem it,
but I was quite the tomboy as a child.

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:04.760
I used to run around these mountains
and play with the animals.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:10.630
You seem like an over-protected,
fragile little princess now.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.190
It was what my father wanted.

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.880
What your father wanted?

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:19.680
And you're fine with that?
What about what you want?

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.570
What I want?

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.220
Well, actually...

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:30.660
Somebody!

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:54.420
There is someone I wish I could see again.

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.920
But it's unlikely.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:20.780
There. No <i>yokai</i> will be able to enter
until sunrise, tomorrow morning.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:24.410
Now all we do is
wait for Hakusanbo, right Kitaro?

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.160
Yes, Dad.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.160
Open up.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.100
HAKUSANBO

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:57.100
Is the owner in?

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.320
Are you Hakusanbo?

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.610
Indeed.

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:05.950
Are you GeGeGe no Kitaro perchance?

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:06.740
Yeah.

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.040
Don't get in my way.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.960
I've come to claim the girl.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:14.200
No. You can't have her.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.750
Why not?

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.060
You plan to eat her, don't you?

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:24.890
Eat the girl? Me?

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:25.720
That's right!

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:28.890
You kidnap and eat humans, don't you?!

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:31.120
That would be my predecessor.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.440
I defeated my predecessor
and took on his name.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.270
I am the sixth Hakusanbo.

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.650
I have no interest in eating humans.

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:43.740
And we should just believe you?

00:09:43.740 --> 00:09:45.860
Wait. Come to think of it...

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:50.320
The Hakusanbo known for eating humans
had only one eye.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.410
Huh? That means...

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:56.210
Exactly.
That was the fifth that I defeated.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:10:01.460
I'm here not to eat the girl,
but to claim her as my bride.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:02.710
Your bride?!

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.090
Indeed.

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:10.740
Ten years ago, that man came to
the mountain I rule to die alone.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:15.020
Your business was failing, you were
swamped with debt, and you wanted to die.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:18.230
That's what you told me then.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:23.690
That's why I offered you wealth.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:30.160
In return, you would give me your
daughter to be my bride when she was 18.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.370
And you agreed to it.

00:10:33.370 --> 00:10:36.250
I used my power as the Hakusanbo

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:40.130
to twist causality and turn your luck
into good fortune.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:43.630
As a result,
you've gained your current wealth!

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:46.800
Observe! This is our contract!

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.510
Now fulfill your promise!

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:53.140
Of course I can't do that!

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:58.100
K-Kitaro-san, defeat this thing!
I'll pay you as much as you like!

00:10:58.100 --> 00:11:02.480
Ooh, that sounds sweet!
Go get him, Kitaro.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:07.230
If that's the case,
you should keep your promise.

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:09.880
Kitaro?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.240
What?! Please, I beg of you!

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:19.460
Kitaro-san, aren't you supposed to be
an ally of humans?!

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:22.040
I'm not anyone's ally.

00:11:23.250 --> 00:11:26.260
The barrier will vanish
at sunrise, tomorrow.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.510
You can take the girl then.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.280
Understood.

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:33.510
I'm to be his bride?

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.520
I'm so sorry, Yayoi...

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:39.810
Kitaro.

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:43.770
He has a contract.
There's nothing we can do.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:45.210
Even so...!

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:50.610
What is this?!

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:51.880
Could it be...?!

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.160
The ring's appeared!

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.450
It's located...

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.200
inside the girl's body!

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:01.980
-My chest...
-Yayoi-san!

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:07.800
I put everything into that barrier.
We can't get close to her.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.350
Adele?!

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:15.320
I'll be taking the ring.

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:21.160
Yayoi!

00:12:22.410 --> 00:12:28.570
I'm sorry, Kitaro. It looks like my
barrier didn't work against Western magic.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.760
It was an unexpected development.
It's not your fault.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:36.070
Explain this, Kitaro.

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:37.570
Right.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:44.380
Buer.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:48.920
Who interrupts my enjoyment?

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.550
DEMON BUER

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:55.180
Save your play time for later.
This is work.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.180
HAKUSANBO

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:03.690
DEMON BUER

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.620
-<i>"Ge."</i>
-<i>"What?"</i>

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:09.690
So she's been caught in a quarrel
between Western <i>yokai</i>?

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:15.620
But if they get their hands on the ring,
this won't be just about Western <i>yokai</i>.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.950
This is our problem, too.

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:22.460
Agnes, is there any way to find
where they teleported to?

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.750
What about your crystal ball?

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:27.250
Adele's cast a concealment spell.
It's no good.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:32.760
They won't hesitate to kill the girl
and extract the ring.

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:36.090
At this rate
the ring will fall into Adele's hands.

00:13:36.090 --> 00:13:37.220
But...

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:39.530
There's a way to follow them.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:44.310
The braid Yayoi is wearing has
my hair woven into it.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:47.480
I can sense its location.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.920
The braid? You mean...

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:51.360
Agnes!

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.290
I'll follow with a teleport spell.

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:56.910
But I can only take one other at the most.

00:13:56.910 --> 00:14:02.370
Then I'll go.
I'm the only one who knows where Yayoi is.

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:05.420
All right. Tell us where she is.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.080
We'll follow right after.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:27.060
There's no mistake.
The ring is behind this girl's heart.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:29.310
Now let's begin.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:39.680
Agnes?!

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:43.470
You bastard! Get your filthy hands
away from Yayoi!

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.500
Are you all right, Yayoi?

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:49.750
Yes.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.210
You would interrupt my operation?

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:54.940
How dare you! How dare you!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:03.800
We're leaving.

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:11.320
Are you all right, Hakusanbo-sama?

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:17.280
A wound like this is nothing.
Worry about yourself.

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.880
Stop!

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:24.410
Hakusanbo-sama!

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.790
Hand over that patient!

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:32.670
No. This girl is mine!

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:37.300
I'll hold him off here.
Take the girl and run!

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.670
But...!

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:40.610
Please.

00:15:42.030 --> 00:15:43.890
All right. Get on!

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:45.180
You're going nowhere!

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:47.850
Oh no you don't!

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:54.440
Hakusanbo-sama!

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:57.440
Damn you're persistent! Take this!

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.950
Why are you doing so much for me?

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:04.080
I made a promise I would make you my wife.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:08.200
Much like your father is bound
by his promise to me,

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:11.210
I, too, am bound by my promise.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:17.250
Protecting one's wife is only natural,
be one a <i>yokai</i> or a human!

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:22.990
<i>Hiroyo yukinotsu!</i>

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:26.950
Let's go!

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:32.660
Dammit!

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.980
You won't take another step!

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:41.860
<i>The ring is inside this girl right now.</i>

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:45.470
<i>If I kill her and take it out,
I'll have the ring.</i>

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:51.350
<i>If it's to stop the Brigadoon Project,
what's the life of one or two humans?</i>

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:54.500
We're speeding up! Hold on tight!

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:57.960
Stop, Agnes!

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:01.340
Hand over that girl, you traitor!

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:02.880
Shut up!

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:08.720
That's far enough!

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.940
Leave this to us! Here!

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:18.060
Is this...?!

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:23.240
It's Paralysis Sand.

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:26.070
While magical logic
may differ between East and West,

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:28.660
medicine still works the same.

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:33.410
Witch, you may have outwitted us earlier,
but not this time.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:37.670
Dammit, dammit! What a persistent patient!

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:40.960
I will protect Yayoi!

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:43.900
Remote Controlled Geta!

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:47.550
Hakusanbo!

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:51.410
You! How dare you!

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:53.180
Damn!

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:01.610
Catchick!

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:03.300
Leave this to me!

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:09.090
There he goes, Kitaro!

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:12.950
Spirit Hair Chanchanko!

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:28.260
Time's up.

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:30.120
The ring's gone.

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:34.520
Buer, that's enough! We're leaving!

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:39.520
I'll dissect you someday.
Remember this, Kitaro!

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:41.920
It's finally over...

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.020
Hakusanbo-sama!

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:50.530
This is the second time
I've gazed up at you like this.

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:54.710
You probably don't remember.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:59.540
Twelve years ago, you saved a lone fox.

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:05.510
It was just after I fought the previous
Hakusanbo who terrorized as a man-eater,

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:08.340
and I'd barely won.

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:14.730
I'd been gravely wounded
and I thought I was going to die.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:17.620
Are you all right, fox-san?

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:26.650
Thanks to your care, I managed to survive.

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:30.970
Since then, I've always watched over you.

00:19:31.550 --> 00:19:37.920
When your father came to the mountain to
die, it seemed like a chance to get close.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:41.920
Then, the one
who saved me that time was...

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.300
When causality is warped,

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:48.670
in exchange for the fortune,
misfortune befalls the surrounding people.

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:52.390
I knew you would become unlucky,

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:57.060
so I tried to protect you
as much as I could.

00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:58.250
Yayoi.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:04.400
If you will accept me,
I swear I'll spend the rest of my life

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:09.050
loving you and protecting you.

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:18.180
You weep in disgust.

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:20.120
Very well then.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.330
Let's forget that--

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:22.630
That's not it.

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.040
I'm happy.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:30.340
I can be the wife of the one
I've been in love with for so long.

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:35.100
I know I'm naive and unskilled,
but if you will have me,

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:36.850
Hakusanbo-sama...

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:10.090
Thank you for everything.

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:13.140
If you ever need my help,
just say the word.

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:17.930
All the Yoko in these mountains
will be at your service.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:35.280
It's less a fox's wedding and more a fox
coming to get his bride, isn't it, Dad?

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:36.490
Indeed.

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:41.870
But, can a human and a <i>yokai</i> marry
and be happy?

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:47.630
Actually, there are lots of stories of
humans marrying foxes since long ago.

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:50.090
There are numerous cases of
them having children.

00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:54.010
I'm sure those two will be happy together.

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:55.200
Huh.

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:56.950
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:57.070 --> 00:21:58.320
<i>Congratulations.</i>

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:00.450
<i>May you find happiness.</i>

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.500
<i>You can't see them
But they're there</i>

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.500
<i>mien keredomo orundayo</i>

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:14.340
<i>"Hello" in the mountains</i>

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:14.340
<i>yama de yahho</i>

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.260
<i>If you call</i>

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:17.260
<i>hitokoe yobeba</i>

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.550
<i>An identical "Hello"</i>

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.550
<i>onaji yahho</i>

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>The Yobuko calls back</i>

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:24.850
<i>yobuko ga kaesu</i>

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.440
<i>A tree spirit living in the mountains</i>

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.440
<i>yama ni sunderu ki no seirei</i>

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.860
<i>A used rag</i>

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:32.860
<i>tsukatta zoukin</i>

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:35.740
<i>If you don't keep it clean</i>

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:35.740
<i>kirei ni shinaito</i>

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:38.110
<i>It'll get smelly</i>

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:38.110
<i>kusaku nattayo</i>

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:43.490
<i>The Shiro-Uneri
Will tangle itself around you</i>

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:43.490
<i>shirouneri karamitsuku</i>

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:46.040
<i>Stuck to your face
How horrible</i>

00:22:43.790 --> 00:22:46.040
<i>kao ni bettori korya tamaran</i>

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:51.540
<i>See how many ghosts there are</i>

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:51.540
<i>konnani oruyo obaketachi</i>

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.090
<i>You can't see them
But they're there</i>

00:22:51.670 --> 00:22:54.090
<i>mien keredomo orundayo</i>

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:59.010
<i>You can't see them
But they're there</i>

00:22:54.210 --> 00:22:59.010
<i>mien keredomo orundayo</i>

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:03.430
<i>They're near you</i>

00:22:59.760 --> 00:23:03.430
<i>kimi no chikaku ni</i>

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:10.060
<i>A black shadow spreads,
swallowing our friends.</i>

00:23:10.190 --> 00:23:12.860
<i>Dad, it feels like
something's watching me...</i>

00:23:12.980 --> 00:23:15.150
<i>Next time on GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:17.400
<i>"Emperor Backbeard"</i>

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:19.990
<i>The door to the unseen world opens...</i>
